                <pb facs="0174" n="78" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg78"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Squiers to the
                            Tsungli Yamen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pekin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic">November 16,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">note verbale.</hi></p>
                <p>The legation of the United States has the honor to inform the Tsungli Yamen that
                    it has just received a telegram from the United States consul at Chefoo, by
                    which it is advised that Rev. W. B. Hamilton, an American missionary residing at
                    Chinanfu, has telegraphed from that place that the Big Knife Society is engaged
                    in burning chapels, looting, and killing Christain converts; that the governor
                    has withdrawn his soldiers, and that the situation is regarded as critical.</p>
                <p>In view of the above report, the legation has to request that the Tsungli Yamen
                    will immediately cause such telegraphic instructions to be given to the governor
                    of Shantung as will insure American citizens living there that full protection
                    in both lives and property to which they are, under the treaties, guaranteed;
                    and, further, that those persons who have been engaged in this disorderly affair
                    be promptly arrested and brought to trial and punished.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
